From: gts7l project
Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: qcom: don't leak lane clock references on resume

ufs_qcom_enable_lane_clks() takes a reference on every clock of the UFS
node (clk_bulk_prepare_enable) and sets is_lane_clks_enabled, and
ufs_qcom_disable_lane_clks() drops one only when that flag is set. The
enable side doesn't check the flag, and system resume calls it twice:
ufshcd_resume() -> ufs_qcom_setup_clocks(on, PRE_CHANGE) with the link in
hibern8, then __ufshcd_wl_resume() -> ufs_qcom_resume(). Each
suspend/resume cycle thus leaks one prepare/enable on core_clk,
bus_aggr_clk, core_clk_unipro and the rest, measured on SM8250: the
gated-state prepare count of gcc_ufs_phy_axi_clk equals the number of
suspends so far.

The leaked references keep GPLL0 running, and GPLL0 keeps the CXO request
asserted, so from the first suspend on the SoC can no longer reach XO
shutdown, AOSS sleep or CX collapse in s2idle.

Make the enable idempotent, like the disable.

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
index 291c43448..c427cc0c9 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -356,6 +356,15 @@ static int ufs_qcom_enable_lane_clks(struct ufs_qcom_host *host)
 {
 	int err;
 
+	/*
+	 * Resume calls this twice (ufs_qcom_setup_clocks() with the link in
+	 * hibern8, then ufs_qcom_resume()), while disable only drops one
+	 * reference: every suspend cycle leaked a prepare on all UFS clocks,
+	 * keeping GPLL0 and so CXO on in s2idle.
+	 */
+	if (host->is_lane_clks_enabled)
+		return 0;
+
 	err = clk_bulk_prepare_enable(host->num_clks, host->clks);
 	if (err)
 		return err;
